# Conditional Workflow Example

This self-contained suite looks up a sensor, accepts either an existing or
missing result, captures the integer response status, conditionally creates the
sensor, and then verifies readiness. Change the lookup mock status from `404`
to `200` to see `sensor-create` skip while `sensor-ready` still runs.

```yaml
variables:
  host: https://api.example.com
  sensor_ref: ${{ random_hex(16) }}
```

## Look Up The Sensor

```yaml
test: sensor-lookup
get: $host/demo/devices/$sensor_ref
mock_only: true
mock:
  status: 404
expect:
  status: [200, 404]
capture:
  sensor_lookup_status: $response.status
```

## Create Only When Missing

```yaml
test: sensor-create
requires: sensor-lookup
when: ${{ sensor_lookup_status == 404 }}
post: $host/demo/devices
body:
  label: DEMO-$sensor_ref
  reference: $sensor_ref
mock_only: true
mock:
  status: 201
  body:
    created: true
expect:
  status: 201
```

## Continue After Create Or Conditional Skip

```yaml
test: sensor-ready
requires:
  - sensor-lookup
  - sensor-create
get: $host/demo/devices/$sensor_ref/status
mock_only: true
mock:
  status: 200
  body:
    ready: true
expect:
  status: 200
  values:
    - key: $.ready
      op: equals
      value: true
```
